From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OneXPlayer 3 / Legion Go 2 OLED: PQ HDR fixes

Applies on top of Anatase's gamescope overrides.patch (gamescope 3.16.23.3, libdisplay-info 0.4.0 packaging).
Squashed from the local gamescope branch oxp3-hdr-min2 (not published):
  - edid: strip DisplayID extensions from the EDID exposed to games (silentsudin)
  - drm: send panel HDR metadata on internal displays (silentsudin)
  - waitable: dispatch EPOLLPRI events to waitables (Matthew Schwartz)
  - DRMBackend: fall back to EDID for HDR luminance metadata when scripts omit it (Matthew Schwartz)
  - scripts: Add Lenovo Legion Go 2 as a known device (Matthew Schwartz)
  - HACK: steamcompmgr: emulate the backlight in software while the output is in PQ (Matthew Schwartz)
  - HACK: scripts: use the software backlight on the Legion Go 2 (Matthew Schwartz)
  - drm: only fill in the panel primaries in internal panel HDR metadata (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: rate-limit content-driven HDR output switches on internal panels (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: optionally keep HDR output on for internal displays (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: space out HDR and VRR modesets on internal displays (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: enable HDR output with VRR off on internal displays (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: enter HDR on internal displays only from SDR with VRR on (silentsudin)
  - drm: send no HDR metadata in SDR on internal displays (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: run VRR while in HDR on internal displays (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: make hdr_force_vrr_internal independent of hdr_enable_via_vrr_internal (silentsudin)
  - drm: fill internal panel HDR luminance metadata from the EDID (silentsudin)
  - steamcompmgr: limit VRR-aware HDR switching to panels that need it (silentsudin)
